d 'POLYCOPULA': module to compute Copula-based association for ordinal variables:  Gaussian (polychoric), Frank, Clayton and Gumbel
d
d      The polychoric correlation is the parameter of a Gaussian
d copula linking the latent variables behind two ordinal variables.
d When	  polytest or the polycorr fit tests reject latent
d normality, the polychoric correlation can misstate the strength
d of association.    polycopula fits, for every pair, the same
d two-step model with the Gaussian copula replaced by:	      o
d Frank: symmetric, no tail dependence;        o Clayton:
d lower-tail dependence;	o Gumbel: upper-tail dependence. 
d
d KW: Copula-based association
d KW: ordinal variables
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author:  Yusuf Toyin Yusuf,  Kwara State University
d Support: email  YUSUF.YUSUF@@KWASU.EDU.NG
d
f polycopula.ado
f polycopula.sthlp
f polycopula_examples.do
f polycopula_cert.do
